# Portability patches (format and list: docs/UPSTREAM_CHANGES.md).
patch: md6-trim-hashval-ptr-decl
why: trim_hashval treats st->hashval as the 128-byte chaining value (c*(w/8)), but the member is hashval[64] (d <= 512 bits).
why: md6_process memcpy's all 128 bytes of the final chaining value into it, so the upper 64 bytes land in the adjacent hexhashval member
why: (same struct, contiguous, no padding), and trim_hashval then indexes st->hashval[64..127] (UBSan: index N out of bounds for unsigned char[64], md6_mode.c:741 and :745).
why: The patch indexes through a plain unsigned char pointer to the same member, so exactly the same bytes are read and written (the last d bits of the chaining value are moved to the front, the rest zeroed); output is unchanged.
why: hv is derived from the whole md6_state object (an unsigned char view of its representation), not from the
why: 64-byte hashval member, so reading its 128 bytes stays inside the object the pointer came from.
file: upstream/ref/md6_mode.c
count: 1
find:   int bits = st->d % 8;                 /* bits in partial byte */
replace:   int bits = st->d % 8;                 /* bits in partial byte */ unsigned char *hv = (unsigned char *)st + ((unsigned char *)st->hashval - (unsigned char *)st);
patch: md6-trim-hashval-ptr-move
why: trim_hashval treats st->hashval as the 128-byte chaining value (c*(w/8)), but the member is hashval[64] (d <= 512 bits).
why: md6_process memcpy's all 128 bytes of the final chaining value into it, so the upper 64 bytes land in the adjacent hexhashval member
why: (same struct, contiguous, no padding), and trim_hashval then indexes st->hashval[64..127] (UBSan: index N out of bounds for unsigned char[64], md6_mode.c:741 and :745).
why: The patch indexes through a plain unsigned char pointer to the same member, so exactly the same bytes are read and written (the last d bits of the chaining value are moved to the front, the rest zeroed); output is unchanged.
file: upstream/ref/md6_mode.c
count: 1
find:     st->hashval[i] = st->hashval[c*(w/8)-full_or_partial_bytes+i];
replace:     hv[i] = hv[c*(w/8)-full_or_partial_bytes+i];
